// 26 U.S.C. Subchapter C of Chapter 63 (§§6221-6241) — Centralized
// partnership audit regime (BBA), stage 2b (25.09.2026, coordinator
// instruction, priority list order).
//
// METHOD NOTE / SCOPE.
//  - §6221(a): the "partnership-level determination" default is modeled as
//    an institutional_effect switch (`partnership_level_determination`)
//    that other rules in this module read; §6221(b): election out for
//    partnerships with 100 or fewer partners is a `power` (holder: the
//    partnership) with the (b)(1)(A)-(E) conditions folded into a single
//    `valid_when` helper relation per the compiler trap (a `power`'s
//    `valid_when` takes exactly one atom). (b)(2) (S-corporation/foreign
//    partner special disclosure rules) is NOT modeled — narrow procedural
//    detail, classified TECH_GAP.
//  - §6222(a): the partner consistency `duty`; (b): the math-error
//    assessment consequence of inconsistency, read as a defeasible
//    classification (assessed the SAME WAY as a math error, not a separate
//    computation); (c): the notification-of-inconsistency defeater. (d),
//    (e) are NOT modeled (procedural detail of the (b) assessment's own
//    restrictions, narrow).
//  - §6223(a): designation of the partnership representative is a `power`
//    (holder: the partnership) whose effect is the institutional fact
//    `partnership_representative_of`; the Secretary's own fallback
//    selection ("In any case in which such a designation is not in
//    effect...") is a SEPARATE power (holder: Secretary) rather than a
//    `priority`-arbitrated pair, because the two are not in genuine
//    conflict (the Secretary's power is conditioned on the ABSENCE of a
//    partnership designation, `not_known`). §6223(b): binding effect is an
//    institutional_effect.
//  - §6225(a)-(c): (a) the general rule (imputed underpayment vs. taken-
//    into-account classification); (b) the actual formula — net POSITIVE
//    partnership adjustments (categories already netted per (b)(3), a
//    modeling simplification: this stage does not compute the netting
//    WITHIN a category from individual line items, it reads the per-
//    category net as a given empirical fact) × the highest rate under
//    section 1 or 11 (an EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY: neither `us.irc.income-
//    individual` nor `us.irc.corporations` exports a single "highest of
//    the two" fact yet, so this package reads the rate as given rather
//    than computing the section-1-vs-section-11 comparison or inventing a
//    number — see TECH-GAPS); (b)(4)'s default disregard of adjustments
//    that would DECREASE the imputed underpayment is modeled by the
//    "positive adjustments only" netting itself (the Secretary's override
//    "except to the extent otherwise provided" is not modeled: TECH_GAP).
//    (c) (modification procedures) is NOT computed — nine paragraphs of
//    Secretary-administered procedure with no self-executing formula for
//    THIS package to run; classified TECH_GAP/NON_NORMATIVE per sub-item,
//    not attempted as executable rules this stage.
//  - §6226(a): the push-out election is a `power` (holder: the
//    partnership), valid only within 45 days of the notice of final
//    partnership adjustment (FPA); effect: §6225 does not apply to the
//    underpayment. (b) (partner-level computation of the pushed-out
//    amounts) is NOT modeled (TECH_GAP — its own multi-year "additional
//    reporting year tax" computation, out of this stage's reach).
//  - §6227(a): filing an administrative adjustment request (AAR) is a
//    `power` (holder: the partnership); (c): the 3-year period of
//    limitations on filing one, plus the "not after a notice of
//    administrative proceeding is mailed" defeater, folded into the same
//    `valid_when` helper. (b) (effect of an AAR) is NOT modeled here
//    (TECH_GAP — its own (b)(1)-(2) branching, out of this stage).
//  - §6231(a)-(b): the three required notices (proceeding, proposed
//    adjustment (NOPPA), final adjustment (FPA)) as institutional facts;
//    (b)(2)(A)'s 270-day minimum gap between NOPPA and FPA as an exact
//    date test (an immunity on the Secretary: the FPA may not be mailed
//    before the 270th day, absent the partnership's waiver — the waiver
//    itself is NOT modeled, TECH_GAP). (c), (d) are NOT modeled this
//    stage (further-notice restriction / rescission — the same shape as
//    `02-deficiency-and-notice.law`'s §6212(c)/(d) but not re-derived
//    here; TECH_GAP, same pattern).
//  - §6232(a)-(b): (a) the imputed underpayment is assessed as if it were
//    a tax for the adjustment year (an institutional_effect linking
//    `imputed_underpayment` to an ordinary `us.irc.core::Assessment`);
//    (b) the immunity: no assessment before the 90th day after the FPA is
//    mailed, and if a §6234 petition is filed, not until the court's
//    decision becomes final (`decision_final_on`, the same pending
//    contract `03-restrictions-and-tax-court.law` already reads).
//  - §6234(a): filing a readjustment petition is a `power` (holder: the
//    partnership), valid within 90 days of the FPA; (b)-(e) (deposit
//    requirement for district-court/Court-of-Federal-Claims petitions,
//    etc.) are NOT modeled (TECH_GAP, narrow venue-specific detail).
//  - §6235(a)-(c): the period of limitations on making an adjustment — 3
//    years from the LATEST of (filing date, return due date, AAR filing
//    date) via the "no strictly later candidate" idiom (TECH-GAPS G136
//    pattern, same as `04-limitations.law`'s carryback chain); (b) the
//    agreement-extension power; (c)(1)-(3) the false-return/no-return
//    "any time" exceptions and the (c)(2) 6-year substantial-omission
//    substitution, mirroring `04-limitations.law`'s own §6501(c)
//    exceptions. (c)(4)-(6) are NOT modeled (cross-references to
//    §6020(b)/§6501(c)(8)/(10), narrow).
//  - §6241: only (1) ("partnership" scope, read from `us.irc.partnerships`'
//    own `is_partner`/entity ontology rather than redefined here), (2)
//    ("partnership adjustment"/"partnership-related item" scope
//    declarations, NON_NORMATIVE definitional aids), and (6)(A) (the
//    title-11 bankruptcy suspension of THIS subchapter's own adjustment
//    period plus the assessment/collection periods it cross-refers to —
//    the coordinator's "(b)-(c)" instruction, mapped onto the ACTUAL
//    paragraph-numbered subsection text pinned in `sources.law`, which
//    uses numbered paragraphs (1)-(12), not lettered subsections (a)-(c);
//    this package does not have a "(b)" or "(c)" to point to and does not
//    invent one) are modeled; the remaining paragraphs ((3)-(5), (7)-(12))
//    are NOT modeled (definitional/administrative, narrow, TECH_GAP or
//    NON_NORMATIVE per coverage row).
//
// This module does NOT model: the (a)(2) partner-level "taken into
// account" mechanics beyond the classification switch, any §6225(c)
// modification procedure, §6226(b)'s partner-level computation, §6231(c)-
// (d), §6232(c)-(f), §6234(b)-(e), and most of §6241's remaining
// paragraphs. Each is a coverage row of its own (TECH_GAP or
// NON_NORMATIVE), not silently dropped.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package us.irc.assessment version "0.1.1";
namespace "urn:us:irc:assessment:clir";

use self::{
    IRC_S6221_A,
    IRC_S6221_B,
    IRC_S6222_A,
    IRC_S6222_B,
    IRC_S6222_C,
    IRC_S6223_A,
    IRC_S6223_B,
    IRC_S6225_A,
    IRC_S6225_B,
    IRC_S6226_A,
    IRC_S6227_A,
    IRC_S6227_C,
    IRC_S6231_A,
    IRC_S6231_B,
    IRC_S6232_A,
    IRC_S6232_B,
    IRC_S6234_A,
    IRC_S6235_A,
    IRC_S6235_B,
    IRC_S6235_C,
    IRC_S6241,
    Partnership,
    Person,
    Proceeding,
    Secretary,
    TaxableYear,
    bankruptcy_case_pending,
    decision_final_on,
    election_out_total_statements,
    fpa_rescinded_with_consent_twin,
    partner_treated_as_notifying_under_6222c2,
    reallocation_adjustment_effect,
    restrictions_waived_twin,
    secretary_permits_decrease_to_be_taken_into_account,
    specified_similar_amount,
    unqualified_s_corporation_partner_exists,
};

// ============================================================================
// §6221 — Determination at partnership level; election out
// ============================================================================

@source(IRC_S6221_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "Any adjustment to a partnership-related item shall be determined, and any tax attributable thereto shall be assessed and collected, and the applicability of any penalty, addition to tax, or additional amount which relates to an adjustment to any such item shall be determined, at the partnership level, except to the extent otherwise provided in this subchapter.")
pub relation partnership_level_determination(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "§6221(a): adjustments to partnership-related items for this partnership taxable year are determined, assessed, and collected at the PARTNERSHIP level (the BBA default), unless the (b) election out applies";
}
pub relation election_out_of_bba_effective(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear) kind institutional;
rule S6221DefaultPartnershipLevelDetermination defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for filedOn: Date;
    when us.irc.partnerships::is_partner(_, pship)
        and partnership_return_filed_on(pship, y, filedOn)
        and not_known(election_out_of_bba_effective(pship, y));
    then partnership_level_determination(pship, y);
}

pub relation election_out_partner_count(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, statements_furnished: Integer) kind empirical {
    label en official "the number of statements the partnership is required to furnish under section 6031(b) with respect to its partners for such taxable year";
}
pub relation election_out_all_partners_eligible_type(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear) kind empirical {
    label en official "each partner of the partnership is an individual, a C corporation, a qualifying foreign entity, an S corporation, or an estate of a deceased partner (section 6221(b)(1)(C))";
}
pub relation election_out_made_with_timely_return(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear) kind empirical {
    label en official "the election is made with a timely filed return for such taxable year and discloses each partner's name and TIN (section 6221(b)(1)(D))";
}
pub relation election_out_partners_notified(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear) kind empirical {
    label en official "the partnership notified each partner of the election in the manner prescribed by the Secretary (section 6221(b)(1)(E))";
}
pub relation election_out_of_bba_conditions_met(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "helper for the power's valid_when (single-atom compiler constraint): all of section 6221(b)(1)(A)-(E) are satisfied, including the <=100-statement threshold of (b)(1)(B)";
}
@source(IRC_S6221_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "for such taxable year the partnership is required to furnish 100 or fewer statements under section 6031(b) with respect to its partners")
rule S6221ElectionOutConditionsMet strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for statements: Integer;
    when election_out_total_statements(pship, y, statements)
        and statements <= 100
        and not_known(unqualified_s_corporation_partner_exists(pship, y))
        and election_out_all_partners_eligible_type(pship, y)
        and election_out_made_with_timely_return(pship, y)
        and election_out_partners_notified(pship, y);
    then election_out_of_bba_conditions_met(pship, y);
}
@source(IRC_S6221_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "This subchapter shall not apply with respect to any partnership for any taxable year if—")
pub rule S6221ElectionOutOfBba defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    when election_out_of_bba_conditions_met(pship, y);
    then power S6221ElectionOutPower {
        holder pship;
        over pship;
        exercise election_out_of_bba_conditions_met(pship, y);
        valid_when election_out_of_bba_conditions_met(pship, y);
        effect create(election_out_of_bba_effective(pship, y));
    };
}
// TECH_GAP: (b)(2)'s special S-corporation-partner and foreign-partner
// disclosure sub-rules (which partners count toward the (b)(1)(B)/(C)
// thresholds) are not modeled — narrow procedural detail layered on top
// of the conditions above, not attempted this stage.

// ============================================================================
// §6222 — Partner's return must be consistent with partnership return
// ============================================================================

pub relation partner_treatment_of_item(partner: Person, pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, item: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the amount at which the partner treated a partnership-related item on the partner's own return (a simplified single-item probe: real §6222 applies item-by-item, this stage models ONE representative item per (partner, partnership, year))";
}
pub relation partnership_treatment_of_item(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, item: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the amount at which the partnership treated the same item on the partnership return";
}
@source(IRC_S6222_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "A partner shall, on the partner's return, treat any partnership-related item in a manner which is consistent with the treatment of such item on the partnership return.")
pub rule S6222ConsistencyDuty defeasible {
    for partner: Person;
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for item: Money;
    when us.irc.partnerships::is_partner(partner, pship) and partnership_treatment_of_item(pship, y, item);
    then duty S6222PartnerConsistencyDuty {
        bearer partner;
        beneficiary Secretary;
        goal maintenance {
            condition partner_treatment_of_item(partner, pship, y, item);
            window [-infinity, infinity];
        }
    };
}
// METHOD NOTE: this duty has no independent statutory deadline of its own
// (it is discharged or breached by the content of the return the partner
// files, not by a separate clock) — modeled as `maintenance`, the same
// idiom `us.irc.alcohol`'s §5555(a) recordkeeping duty uses for a
// standing conduct requirement rather than a one-time achievement by a
// date; `partner_treatment_inconsistent` (below) is the breach-detecting
// counterpart a consumer reads instead of testing this duty's own VIOLATED
// state directly (E-0179: no bare negation of an empirical condition).

pub relation partner_notified_secretary_of_inconsistency(partner: Person, pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, item: Money) kind empirical {
    label en official "the partner files with the Secretary a statement identifying the inconsistency (section 6222(c)(1)(B))";
}
pub relation partner_treatment_inconsistent(partner: Person, pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, item: Money) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "the partner's treatment of the item does not match the partnership's treatment (section 6222(a)/(b) predicate)";
}
rule S6222TreatmentInconsistentDetected strict {
    for partner: Person;
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for partnerAmount: Money;
    for pshipAmount: Money;
    when partner_treatment_of_item(partner, pship, y, partnerAmount)
        and partnership_treatment_of_item(pship, y, pshipAmount)
        and partnerAmount != pshipAmount;
    then partner_treatment_inconsistent(partner, pship, y, partnerAmount);
}
@source(IRC_S6222_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "Any underpayment of tax by a partner by reason of failing to comply with the requirements of subsection (a) shall be assessed and collected in the same manner as if such underpayment were on account of a mathematical or clerical error appearing on the partner's return.")
pub rule S6222InconsistentUnderpaymentAssessedAsMathError defeasible {
    for partner: Person;
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for item: Money;
    when partner_treatment_inconsistent(partner, pship, y, item)
        and not_known(partner_notified_secretary_of_inconsistency(partner, pship, y, item))
        and not_known(partner_treated_as_notifying_under_6222c2(partner, pship, y, item));
    then assessed_as_math_or_clerical_error(partner, y);
}
pub relation assessed_as_math_or_clerical_error(p: Person, y: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "the underpayment is assessed and collected as though it were a section 6213(b)(1) mathematical or clerical error — NOT itself a `math_error_notice_given` fact (that relation carries the notice's own required content under 03-restrictions-and-tax-court.law); a consumer needing the actual notice mechanics composes the two facts, this rule only classifies the assessment as math-error-like per section 6222(b)'s own text ('Paragraph (2) of section 6213(b) shall not apply', i.e. no 60-day abatement right for THIS kind of math-error assessment)";
}
@source(IRC_S6222_C, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "the partner files with the Secretary a statement identifying the inconsistency,")
rule S6222NotificationDefeatsConsistencyDutyAndMathErrorTreatment strict {
    for partner: Person;
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for item: Money;
    when partner_notified_secretary_of_inconsistency(partner, pship, y, item);
    then notification_of_inconsistency_filed(partner, pship, y, item);
}
pub relation notification_of_inconsistency_filed(partner: Person, pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, item: Money) kind institutional;
// TECH_GAP: §6222(c)(2) (partner receiving incorrect information from the
// partnership is treated as having complied with (c)(1)(B)) and (d)-(e)
// are not modeled — narrow procedural extensions of the (c) defeater.

// ============================================================================
// §6223 — Partnership representative
// ============================================================================

pub relation partnership_designates_representative(pship: Partnership, rep: Person, designatedOn: Date) kind empirical {
    label en official "the partnership designates (in the manner prescribed by the Secretary) a partner or other person with a substantial presence in the United States as the partnership representative";
}
pub relation representative_has_substantial_us_presence(rep: Person) kind empirical {
    label en official "the designee has a substantial presence in the United States, as section 6223(a) requires of the partnership representative";
}
pub relation partnership_representative_of(pship: Partnership, rep: Person) kind institutional {
    label en official "the partnership representative, who has the sole authority to act on behalf of the partnership under this subchapter";
}
pub relation representative_designation_valid(pship: Partnership, rep: Person) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "helper for valid_when: the designee has a substantial U.S. presence (single-atom compiler constraint)";
}
rule S6223DesignationValid strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for rep: Person;
    for designatedOn: Date;
    when partnership_designates_representative(pship, rep, designatedOn)
        and representative_has_substantial_us_presence(rep);
    then representative_designation_valid(pship, rep);
}
@source(IRC_S6223_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "Each partnership shall designate (in the manner prescribed by the Secretary) a partner (or other person) with a substantial presence in the United States as the partnership representative who shall have the sole authority to act on behalf of the partnership under this subchapter.")
pub rule S6223DesignateRepresentative defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for rep: Person;
    for designatedOn: Date;
    when partnership_designates_representative(pship, rep, designatedOn);
    then power S6223DesignateRepresentativePower {
        holder pship;
        over rep;
        exercise partnership_designates_representative(pship, rep, designatedOn);
        valid_when representative_designation_valid(pship, rep);
        effect create(partnership_representative_of(pship, rep));
    };
}
@source(IRC_S6223_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "In any case in which such a designation is not in effect, the Secretary may select any person as the partnership representative.")
pub relation representative_designated_for(pship: Partnership) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "existential wrapper (§14/§98 idiom: `_` is only a positive-literal argument, never usable under `not_known`) over `partnership_representative_of` — bound the ordinary way so the Secretary's fallback-selection condition below can test its ABSENCE";
}
rule S6223RepresentativeDesignatedExists strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for rep: Person;
    when partnership_representative_of(pship, rep);
    then representative_designated_for(pship);
}
pub relation secretary_selects_representative(pship: Partnership, rep: Person) kind empirical;
pub relation secretary_selection_no_designation_in_effect(pship: Partnership) kind institutional;
rule S6223SecretarySelectionConditionMet defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for rep: Person;
    when secretary_selects_representative(pship, rep)
        and not_known(representative_designated_for(pship));
    then secretary_selection_no_designation_in_effect(pship);
}
pub rule S6223SecretarySelectsRepresentativeWhenNoneDesignated defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for rep: Person;
    when secretary_selects_representative(pship, rep);
    then power S6223SecretarySelectsRepresentativePower {
        holder Secretary;
        over pship;
        exercise secretary_selects_representative(pship, rep);
        valid_when secretary_selection_no_designation_in_effect(pship);
        effect create(partnership_representative_of(pship, rep));
    };
}
@source(IRC_S6223_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "A partnership and all partners of such partnership shall be bound—")
pub rule S6223BindingEffectOnPartnership strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for rep: Person;
    when partnership_representative_of(pship, rep);
    then bound_by_representative_actions(pship);
}
pub relation bound_by_representative_actions(pship: Partnership) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "section 6223(b): the partnership and all its partners are bound by the representative's actions under this subchapter and by any final decision in a subchapter proceeding — this stage marks the institutional effect on the PARTNERSHIP; extending it to each individual partner is a further fact a consumer derives from `us.irc.partnerships::is_partner`, not duplicated here";
}

// ============================================================================
// §6225 — Partnership adjustment: imputed underpayment
// ============================================================================

pub enum PartnershipAdjustmentCategory {
    IncomeGainLossOrDeductionItems;    // items separately stated under section 702(a)
    CreditItems;
    OtherSeparatelyStatedItems;
    label en unofficial "the section 6225(b)(3) categories within which partnership adjustments are separately netted before being combined";
}
pub relation partnership_adjustment_item(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear, category: PartnershipAdjustmentCategory, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the ALREADY-NETTED adjustment amount within one section 6225(b)(3) category for the reviewed year (a positive amount increases, a negative amount decreases, the imputed underpayment before the (b)(4) limitation); this stage does not compute the netting of individual line items INTO this per-category figure — that arithmetic is read as given";
}
pub relation net_positive_partnership_adjustments(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear, total: Money) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "section 6225(b)(1)(A)/(b)(4): the sum of only the POSITIVE per-category net adjustments (a negative-adjustment category is disregarded by default, per (b)(4), absent the Secretary's contrary determination under the final clause of (b)(4) — not modeled, TECH_GAP)";
}
rule S6225NetPositiveAdjustments defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for reviewedYear: TaxableYear;
    when exists_partnership_adjustment_for_year(pship, reviewedYear);
    then net_positive_partnership_adjustments(pship, reviewedYear,
        max(
            (sum all amount: Money for category: PartnershipAdjustmentCategory
                where partnership_adjustment_item(pship, reviewedYear, category, amount) and amount > 0.00 USD)
            + (sum all amount: Money for category: PartnershipAdjustmentCategory
                where partnership_adjustment_item(pship, reviewedYear, category, amount)
                    and amount < 0.00 USD
                    and secretary_permits_decrease_to_be_taken_into_account(pship, reviewedYear, category))
            + (sum all amount: Money for category: PartnershipAdjustmentCategory
                where reallocation_adjustment_effect(pship, reviewedYear, category, amount) and amount > 0.00 USD),
            0.00 USD));
}
pub relation exists_partnership_adjustment_for_year(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear) kind institutional;
rule S6225ExistsAdjustment strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for reviewedYear: TaxableYear;
    for category: PartnershipAdjustmentCategory;
    for amount: Money;
    when partnership_adjustment_item(pship, reviewedYear, category, amount);
    then exists_partnership_adjustment_for_year(pship, reviewedYear);
}

pub relation applicable_highest_rate_for_reviewed_year(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear, rate: Decimal) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "section 6225(b)(1)(B): the highest rate of tax in effect for the reviewed year under section 1 or 11 — a typed dependency on us.irc.income-individual's section 1(j)(2)(A) top individual rate and us.irc.corporations' section 11(b) flat rate (corporate_tax_rate); neither package exports a single 'highest of the two' fact yet, so this relation is read as GIVEN rather than computed (never invented) — see TECH-GAPS";
}
// WIRE-4 (26.09.2026): the section 11 half of "the highest rate of tax in
// effect for the reviewed year under section 1 or 11" is read from
// `us.irc.corporations::maximum_section_11b_rate` (keyed by the year alone);
// the section 1 half stays a case-supplied contract fact, because
// `us.irc.income_individual` exports no single "top individual rate" relation
// (DECISIONS Д-11). The comparison "highest of the two" is the norm itself.
// The relation above remains a valid channel: a case that asserts it directly
// (the older scenarios) is unchanged; a case must not assert both channels.
@source(IRC_S6225_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "applying the highest rate of tax in effect for the reviewed year under section 1 or 11.")
pub relation highest_section_1_rate_for_reviewed_year(reviewedYear: TaxableYear, rate: Decimal) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the highest rate of tax in effect for the reviewed year under section 1 (section 1(j)(2)(A) for years covered by it) — a dependency contract fact: us.irc.income_individual does not export a single top-rate relation";
}
@source(IRC_S6225_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "applying the highest rate of tax in effect for the reviewed year under section 1 or 11.")
rule S6225HighestRateUnderSection1Or11(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear, r1: Decimal, r11: Decimal) strict {
    label en official "section 6225(b)(1)(B): the applicable rate is the higher of the section 1 top rate (contract fact) and the section 11 rate read from the corporations owner";
    when exists_partnership_adjustment_for_year(pship, reviewedYear);
    when highest_section_1_rate_for_reviewed_year(reviewedYear, r1);
    when us.irc.corporations::maximum_section_11b_rate(reviewedYear, r11);
    then applicable_highest_rate_for_reviewed_year(pship, reviewedYear, max(r1, r11));
}
@source(IRC_S6225_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "if such adjustments result in an imputed underpayment, the partnership shall pay an amount equal to such imputed underpayment in the adjustment year as provided in section 6232")
pub relation imputed_underpayment(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "section 6225(a)(1)/(b)(1): the imputed underpayment for the reviewed year — net positive partnership adjustments times the applicable highest rate";
}
@source(IRC_S6225_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "any imputed underpayment with respect to any reviewed year shall be determined by the Secretary by—")
pub rule S6225DetermineImputedUnderpayment defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for reviewedYear: TaxableYear;
    for netPositive: Money;
    for rate: Decimal;
    when net_positive_partnership_adjustments(pship, reviewedYear, netPositive)
        and applicable_highest_rate_for_reviewed_year(pship, reviewedYear, rate)
        and netPositive > 0.00 USD;
    then imputed_underpayment(pship, reviewedYear, round(netPositive * rate, 2, "HALF_UP"));
}
@source(IRC_S6225_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "if such adjustments do not result in an imputed underpayment, such adjustments shall be taken into account by the partnership in the adjustment year.")
pub rule S6225AdjustmentsNotResultingInUnderpaymentTakenIntoAccount defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for reviewedYear: TaxableYear;
    for netPositive: Money;
    when net_positive_partnership_adjustments(pship, reviewedYear, netPositive)
        and netPositive == 0.00 USD;
    then adjustments_taken_into_account_in_adjustment_year(pship, reviewedYear);
}
pub relation adjustments_taken_into_account_in_adjustment_year(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "section 6225(a)(2): a classification switch only — HOW the adjustment year return reflects these adjustments is not computed by this package (the partnership's own adjustment-year return mechanics belong to `us.irc.partnerships`, not modeled here)";
}
// TECH_GAP: section 6225(c) (nine paragraphs of Secretary-administered
// modification procedures: amended-return credit, tax-exempt-partner
// exclusion, lower-rate demonstration, publicly-traded-partnership passive
// losses) has no self-executing formula for this package to run — the
// Secretary's approval under (c)(8) is itself the operative act, not a
// computation. Classified TECH_GAP/NON_NORMATIVE per coverage row, not
// attempted as executable rules.

// ============================================================================
// §6226 — Alternative to payment of imputed underpayment (push-out election)
// ============================================================================

pub relation notice_of_final_partnership_adjustment_mailed(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear, mailedOn: Date) kind empirical {
    label en official "the date of the notice of final partnership adjustment (FPA) under section 6231(a)(3)";
}
pub relation push_out_election_made(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear, madeOn: Date) kind empirical {
    label en official "the partnership elects the application of section 6226 with respect to an imputed underpayment and furnishes each partner's statement of adjustment share";
}
pub relation push_out_election_timely(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "helper for valid_when: the election is made not later than 45 days after the date of the FPA (single-atom compiler constraint)";
}
rule S6226PushOutElectionTimely strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for reviewedYear: TaxableYear;
    for mailedOn: Date;
    for madeOn: Date;
    when notice_of_final_partnership_adjustment_mailed(pship, reviewedYear, mailedOn)
        and push_out_election_made(pship, reviewedYear, madeOn)
        and madeOn <= add_calendar_period(mailedOn, 45 calendar_day);
    then push_out_election_timely(pship, reviewedYear);
}
pub relation push_out_election_valid(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en official "section 6225 shall not apply with respect to the imputed underpayment (no assessment, levy, or collection proceeding against the partnership for it), and each partner takes the adjustment into account instead";
}
@source(IRC_S6226_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "not later than 45 days after the date of the notice of final partnership adjustment, elects the application of this section with respect to an imputed underpayment")
pub rule S6226PushOutElection defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for reviewedYear: TaxableYear;
    for madeOn: Date;
    when push_out_election_made(pship, reviewedYear, madeOn);
    then power S6226PushOutElectionPower {
        holder pship;
        over pship;
        exercise push_out_election_made(pship, reviewedYear, madeOn);
        valid_when push_out_election_timely(pship, reviewedYear);
        effect create(push_out_election_valid(pship, reviewedYear));
    };
}
// TECH_GAP: section 6226(b) (each partner's own additional reporting-year
// tax computed from the pushed-out adjustment share, including the (b)(2)
// interest and (b)(3)-(4) special rules) is not modeled — a further,
// separate multi-step computation this stage does not reach.

// ============================================================================
// §6227 — Administrative adjustment request (AAR) by the partnership
// ============================================================================

pub relation administrative_adjustment_request_filed(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, filedOn: Date) kind empirical {
    label en official "a request for an administrative adjustment in the amount of one or more partnership-related items for the partnership taxable year";
}
pub relation partnership_return_filed_on(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, filedOn: Date) kind empirical;
pub relation partnership_return_due_date(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, dueOn: Date) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the last day for filing the partnership return for such year, determined without regard to extensions (section 6227(c)(1)/(2) reference point)";
}
pub relation notice_of_administrative_proceeding_mailed(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, mailedOn: Date) kind empirical {
    label en official "a notice of an administrative proceeding with respect to the taxable year mailed under section 6231";
}
pub relation exists_administrative_proceeding_notice(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "existential wrapper (`_` is only a positive-literal argument, §14/§98) over `notice_of_administrative_proceeding_mailed`, so its ABSENCE can be tested by `not_known`";
}
rule S6227AdministrativeProceedingNoticeExists strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for mailedOn: Date;
    when notice_of_administrative_proceeding_mailed(pship, y, mailedOn);
    then exists_administrative_proceeding_notice(pship, y);
}
pub relation aar_period_of_limitations_open(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, filedOn: Date) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "helper for valid_when: the AAR is filed not more than 3 years after the later of the return-filing date or its due date, and no notice of an administrative proceeding has been mailed first (single-atom compiler constraint)";
}
@source(IRC_S6227_C, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "A partnership may not file such a request more than 3 years after the later of—")
rule S6227AarPeriodOpenFromFilingDate strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for filedOn: Date;
    for returnFiledOn: Date;
    for dueOn: Date;
    when administrative_adjustment_request_filed(pship, y, filedOn)
        and partnership_return_filed_on(pship, y, returnFiledOn)
        and partnership_return_due_date(pship, y, dueOn)
        and returnFiledOn >= dueOn
        and filedOn <= add_calendar_period(returnFiledOn, 3 calendar_year)
        and not_known(exists_administrative_proceeding_notice(pship, y));
    then aar_period_of_limitations_open(pship, y, filedOn);
}
@source(IRC_S6227_C, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "A partnership may not file such a request more than 3 years after the later of—")
rule S6227AarPeriodOpenFromDueDate strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for filedOn: Date;
    for returnFiledOn: Date;
    for dueOn: Date;
    when administrative_adjustment_request_filed(pship, y, filedOn)
        and partnership_return_filed_on(pship, y, returnFiledOn)
        and partnership_return_due_date(pship, y, dueOn)
        and dueOn > returnFiledOn
        and filedOn <= add_calendar_period(dueOn, 3 calendar_year)
        and not_known(exists_administrative_proceeding_notice(pship, y));
    then aar_period_of_limitations_open(pship, y, filedOn);
}
@source(IRC_S6227_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "A partnership may file a request for an administrative adjustment in the amount of one or more partnership-related items for any partnership taxable year.")
pub rule S6227FileAdministrativeAdjustmentRequest defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for filedOn: Date;
    when administrative_adjustment_request_filed(pship, y, filedOn);
    then power S6227FileAarPower {
        holder pship;
        over pship;
        exercise administrative_adjustment_request_filed(pship, y, filedOn);
        valid_when aar_period_of_limitations_open(pship, y, filedOn);
        effect create(aar_timely_filed(pship, y, filedOn));
    };
}
pub relation aar_timely_filed(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, filedOn: Date) kind institutional;
pub relation exists_aar_timely_filed(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "existential wrapper over `aar_timely_filed` for `not_known` (§14/§98: `_` is only a positive-literal argument)";
}
rule S6227ExistsAarTimelyFiled strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for filedOn: Date;
    when aar_timely_filed(pship, y, filedOn);
    then exists_aar_timely_filed(pship, y);
}
// TECH_GAP: section 6227(b) (the AAR's own effect — (b)(1) treated as if
// it were an imputed underpayment paid with the request, (b)(2) partners
// take the adjustment into account) is not modeled this stage.

// ============================================================================
// §6231 — Notice of proceedings and adjustments
// ============================================================================

pub relation notice_of_administrative_proceeding_for(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, mailedOn: Date) kind institutional;
rule S6231NoticeOfProceedingMailed strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for mailedOn: Date;
    when notice_of_administrative_proceeding_mailed(pship, y, mailedOn);
    then notice_of_administrative_proceeding_for(pship, y, mailedOn);
}
pub relation notice_of_proposed_partnership_adjustment_mailed(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, mailedOn: Date) kind empirical {
    label en official "notice of a proposed partnership adjustment (NOPPA) resulting from the proceeding";
}
@source(IRC_S6231_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "The Secretary shall mail to the partnership and the partnership representative—")
pub rule S6231RequiredNoticesMailedToRepresentative strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for rep: Person;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for mailedOn: Date;
    when partnership_representative_of(pship, rep)
        and notice_of_administrative_proceeding_for(pship, y, mailedOn);
    then notice_mailed_to_representative(pship, rep, y, mailedOn);
}
pub relation notice_mailed_to_representative(pship: Partnership, rep: Person, y: TaxableYear, mailedOn: Date) kind institutional;

pub relation notice_of_final_partnership_adjustment_immune_before_270_days(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "helper for the immunity's window: derived only as a marker so the immunity rule below can name a single institutional predicate as its trigger, per this package's own §6213(a)-style pattern (03-restrictions-and-tax-court.law)";
}
rule S6231NoppaMailedTriggersMinimumGap strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for noppaOn: Date;
    when notice_of_proposed_partnership_adjustment_mailed(pship, y, noppaOn);
    then notice_of_final_partnership_adjustment_immune_before_270_days(pship, y);
}
@source(IRC_S6231_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "Except to the extent that the partnership elects to waive the application of this subparagraph, any notice of a final partnership adjustment shall not be mailed earlier than 270 days after the date on which the notice of the proposed partnership adjustment is mailed.")
pub rule S6231FpaBarredBefore270DaysAfterNoppa defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for noppaOn: Date;
    for attemptedOn: Date;
    when notice_of_proposed_partnership_adjustment_mailed(pship, y, noppaOn)
        and notice_of_final_partnership_adjustment_mailed(pship, y, attemptedOn)
        and attemptedOn < add_calendar_period(noppaOn, 270 calendar_day);
    then immunity S6231FpaMinimumGapImmunity {
        holder pship;
        protected_effect fpa_effective(pship, y, attemptedOn);
        window [noppaOn, add_calendar_period(noppaOn, 270 calendar_day)];
    };
}
pub relation fpa_effective(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, mailedOn: Date) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "the FPA takes effect for purposes of the notices this subchapter conditions on it (e.g. section 6232(b)'s 90-day assessment bar, section 6234(a)'s 90-day petition window) — blocked while the section 6231(b)(2)(A) immunity above applies";
}
rule S6231FpaEffectiveWhenNotBarred defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for mailedOn: Date;
    when notice_of_final_partnership_adjustment_mailed(pship, y, mailedOn);
    then fpa_effective(pship, y, mailedOn);
    unless fpa_rescinded_with_consent_twin(pship, y, mailedOn);
}
// TECH_GAP: (a)(3)'s independent FPA-mailing fact is folded into
// `notice_of_final_partnership_adjustment_mailed` (already declared in the
// §6226 section above, reused here rather than redeclared). (c) (further-
// notice restriction after a §6234 petition) and (d) (rescission with
// consent) are NOT modeled — the same shape as §6212(c)/(d) already
// modeled for individual deficiency notices, not re-derived for the BBA
// notice family this stage.

// ============================================================================
// §6232 — Assessment, collection, and payment
// ============================================================================

@source(IRC_S6232_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "Any imputed underpayment shall be assessed and collected in the same manner as if it were a tax imposed for the adjustment year by subtitle A")
pub rule S6232AssessImputedUnderpaymentAsAdjustmentYearTax defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for reviewedYear: TaxableYear;
    for adjustmentYear: TaxableYear;
    for amount: Money;
    when imputed_underpayment(pship, reviewedYear, amount)
        and adjustment_year_for_reviewed_year(pship, reviewedYear, adjustmentYear);
    then imputed_underpayment_assessable_for_adjustment_year(pship, adjustmentYear, amount);
}
pub relation adjustment_year_for_reviewed_year(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear, adjustmentYear: TaxableYear) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the section 6225(d)/6241 'adjustment year' corresponding to the reviewed year (the year in which the FPA becomes final, mailed, or otherwise fixed) — read as given; this package does not itself compute which taxable year is the adjustment year";
}
pub relation imputed_underpayment_assessable_for_adjustment_year(pship: Partnership, adjustmentYear: TaxableYear, amount: Money) kind institutional;

pub relation partnership_adjustment_final(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en official "section 6232(b): the imputed underpayment is no longer immune from assessment/collection — either the 90-day window after the FPA has closed with no section 6234 petition on file, or (if a petition was filed) the court's decision has become final";
}
@source(IRC_S6232_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "no assessment of an imputed underpayment may be made (and no levy or proceeding in any court for the collection of any amount resulting from such adjustment may be made, begun or prosecuted) before—")
pub rule S6232ImmuneFromAssessmentBeforeNinetyDaysAndPendingDecision defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for reviewedYear: TaxableYear;
    for mailedOn: Date;
    for attemptedOn: Date;
    for similarAmount: Money;
    when fpa_effective(pship, reviewedYear, mailedOn)
        and attempted_assessment_of_imputed_underpayment(pship, reviewedYear, attemptedOn)
        and attemptedOn < add_calendar_period(mailedOn, 90 calendar_day);
    then immunity S6232NinetyDayImmunity {
        holder pship;
        protected_effect attempted_assessment_of_imputed_underpayment(pship, reviewedYear, attemptedOn);
        window [mailedOn, add_calendar_period(mailedOn, 90 calendar_day)];
    };
    unless restrictions_waived_twin(pship, reviewedYear) and fpa_effective(pship, reviewedYear, mailedOn) and attempted_assessment_of_imputed_underpayment(pship, reviewedYear, attemptedOn);
    unless specified_similar_amount(pship, reviewedYear, similarAmount) and fpa_effective(pship, reviewedYear, mailedOn) and attempted_assessment_of_imputed_underpayment(pship, reviewedYear, attemptedOn);
}
pub relation attempted_assessment_of_imputed_underpayment(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear, attemptedOn: Date) kind empirical;
pub relation finality_check_as_of(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear, asOf: Date) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the date as of which section 6232(b) finality is being tested (a case-supplied anchor, not a computed 'now' — this package has no 'current date' primitive; see report judgment call)";
}
rule S6232FinalAfterNinetyDaysNoPetition defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for reviewedYear: TaxableYear;
    for mailedOn: Date;
    for asOf: Date;
    when fpa_effective(pship, reviewedYear, mailedOn)
        and finality_check_as_of(pship, reviewedYear, asOf)
        and not_known(exists_readjustment_petition_filed_timely(pship, reviewedYear))
        and asOf >= add_calendar_period(mailedOn, 90 calendar_day);
    then partnership_adjustment_final(pship, reviewedYear);
}
rule S6232FinalAfterCourtDecisionFinal defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for reviewedYear: TaxableYear;
    for pr: Proceeding;
    for finalOn: Date;
    when readjustment_petition_filed_timely(pship, reviewedYear, pr)
        and decision_final_on(pr, finalOn);
    then partnership_adjustment_final(pship, reviewedYear);
}
// TECH_GAP: (a)(1) ("subchapter B of chapter 63 shall not apply") and
// (a)(2) (AAR-imputed-underpayment paid-with-request timing), and (c)-(f)
// (interest, specified similar amounts, tax attributes, definitions) are
// not modeled. `S6232FinalAfterNinetyDaysNoPetition`'s use of `today` (a
// case-supplied "as of" date, not a computed constant) is the same idiom
// this package uses nowhere else for a strict rule — flagged as a
// judgment call in the report, not silently presented as parallel to the
// immunity's own `window` mechanism.

// ============================================================================
// §6234 — Judicial review of partnership adjustment
// ============================================================================

pub relation readjustment_petition_filed(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear, pr: Proceeding, filedOn: Date) kind empirical {
    label en official "the partnership files a petition for a readjustment with the Tax Court, a district court, or the Court of Federal Claims";
}
pub relation readjustment_petition_timely(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "helper for valid_when: filed within 90 days after the FPA is mailed (single-atom compiler constraint)";
}
rule S6234PetitionTimely defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for reviewedYear: TaxableYear;
    for mailedOn: Date;
    for pr: Proceeding;
    for filedOn: Date;
    when fpa_effective(pship, reviewedYear, mailedOn)
        and readjustment_petition_filed(pship, reviewedYear, pr, filedOn)
        and filedOn <= add_calendar_period(mailedOn, 90 calendar_day);
    then readjustment_petition_timely(pship, reviewedYear);
}
@source(IRC_S6234_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "Within 90 days after the date on which a notice of a final partnership adjustment is mailed under section 6231 with respect to any partnership taxable year, the partnership may file a petition for a readjustment for such taxable year with—")
pub rule S6234FileReadjustmentPetition defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for reviewedYear: TaxableYear;
    for pr: Proceeding;
    for filedOn: Date;
    when readjustment_petition_filed(pship, reviewedYear, pr, filedOn);
    then power S6234FileReadjustmentPetitionPower {
        holder pship;
        over pship;
        exercise readjustment_petition_filed(pship, reviewedYear, pr, filedOn);
        valid_when readjustment_petition_timely(pship, reviewedYear);
        effect create(readjustment_petition_filed_timely(pship, reviewedYear, pr));
    };
}
pub relation readjustment_petition_filed_timely(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear, pr: Proceeding) kind institutional;
pub relation exists_readjustment_petition_filed_timely(pship: Partnership, reviewedYear: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "existential wrapper over `readjustment_petition_filed_timely` for `not_known` (§14/§98: `_` is only a positive-literal argument)";
}
rule S6234ExistsReadjustmentPetitionFiledTimely strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for reviewedYear: TaxableYear;
    for pr: Proceeding;
    when readjustment_petition_filed_timely(pship, reviewedYear, pr);
    then exists_readjustment_petition_filed_timely(pship, reviewedYear);
}
// TECH_GAP: (b) (the deposit jurisdictional requirement for district
// court/Court of Federal Claims petitions), (c)-(e) are not modeled.

// ============================================================================
// §6235 — Period of limitations on making adjustments
// ============================================================================

pub relation bba_adjustment_made_on(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, madeOn: Date) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the date the Secretary makes an adjustment under this subchapter for the partnership taxable year (proxied here by the date the FPA is mailed, since the adjustment is fixed by that notice)";
}
pub relation bba_no_later_candidate_than_filing(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "helper for the section 6235(a)(1) 'later of' idiom (TECH-GAPS G136 pattern): no candidate among (return filed, return due, AAR filed) is strictly LATER than the return-filed candidate";
}
rule S6235FilingDateIsLatestCandidate defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for filedOn: Date;
    for dueOn: Date;
    when partnership_return_filed_on(pship, y, filedOn)
        and partnership_return_due_date(pship, y, dueOn)
        and filedOn >= dueOn
        and not_known(exists_aar_timely_filed(pship, y));
    then bba_no_later_candidate_than_filing(pship, y);
}
@source(IRC_S6235_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "no adjustment under this subchapter for any partnership taxable year may be made after the later of—")
pub rule S6235AdjustmentPeriodEndsThreeYearsFromFiling defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for filedOn: Date;
    when bba_no_later_candidate_than_filing(pship, y)
        and partnership_return_filed_on(pship, y, filedOn);
    then bba_adjustment_period_ends(pship, y, add_calendar_period(filedOn, 3 calendar_year));
}
pub relation bba_adjustment_period_ends(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, d: Date) kind institutional {
    label en official "section 6235(a): the date after which no adjustment under this subchapter may be made for this partnership taxable year";
}
@source(IRC_S6235_C, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "In the case of a false or fraudulent partnership return with intent to evade tax, the adjustment may be made at any time.")
pub relation partnership_false_or_fraudulent_return(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "DECISION-0194 evaluative element (fraud, intent to evade), channeled as an external judgment relation with authority the Tax Court — the same simplification `04-limitations.law` already flags for the individual (c)(1) exception";
}
@source(IRC_S6235_C, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "In the case of a failure by a partnership to file a return for any taxable year, the adjustment may be made at any time.")
pub relation partnership_no_return_filed(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear) kind empirical;
@source(IRC_S6235_C, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "If any partnership omits from gross income an amount properly includible therein and such amount is described in subparagraph (A) or (C) of section 6501(e)(1), subsection (a) shall be applied by substituting \"6 years\" for \"3 years\".")
pub relation partnership_substantial_omission_from_gross_income(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "mirrors `substantial_omission_from_gross_income` in 04-limitations.law for an individual return; not re-derived from a shared relation here (a partnership return's gross-income omission is a separate fact pattern this stage reads as given, not computed from partnership-level items)";
}
rule S6235SixYearPeriodForSubstantialOmission defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for filedOn: Date;
    when bba_no_later_candidate_than_filing(pship, y)
        and partnership_substantial_omission_from_gross_income(pship, y)
        and partnership_return_filed_on(pship, y, filedOn);
    then bba_adjustment_period_ends(pship, y, add_calendar_period(filedOn, 6 calendar_year));
}
pub relation bba_adjustment_period_unlimited(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear) kind institutional {
    label en official "section 6235(c)(1)/(3): no period of limitations applies — a false/fraudulent return or a failure to file";
}
rule S6235UnlimitedForFraud defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    when partnership_false_or_fraudulent_return(pship, y);
    then bba_adjustment_period_unlimited(pship, y);
}
rule S6235UnlimitedForNoReturn defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    when partnership_no_return_filed(pship, y);
    then bba_adjustment_period_unlimited(pship, y);
}
pub relation bba_period_extension_agreed(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, until: Date, agreedOn: Date) kind empirical {
    label en official "an agreement entered into by the Secretary and the partnership, before the expiration of the section 6235(a) period, extending it to `until`";
}
pub relation bba_extension_within_original_period(pship: Partnership, y: TaxableYear, until: Date, agreedOn: Date) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "helper for valid_when: the agreement was entered into before the then-running period expired (single-atom compiler constraint)";
}
rule S6235ExtensionWithinOriginalPeriod defeasible {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for until: Date;
    for agreedOn: Date;
    for periodEnd: Date;
    when bba_period_extension_agreed(pship, y, until, agreedOn)
        and bba_adjustment_period_ends(pship, y, periodEnd)
        and agreedOn <= periodEnd
        and until > periodEnd;
    then bba_extension_within_original_period(pship, y, until, agreedOn);
}
@source(IRC_S6235_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "The period described in subsection (a) (including an extension period under this subsection) may be extended by an agreement entered into by the Secretary and the partnership before the expiration of such period.")
pub rule S6235ExtendAdjustmentPeriodByAgreement strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for until: Date;
    for agreedOn: Date;
    when bba_extension_within_original_period(pship, y, until, agreedOn);
    then power S6235ExtendByAgreementPower {
        holder Secretary;
        over pship;
        exercise bba_period_extension_agreed(pship, y, until, agreedOn);
        valid_when bba_extension_within_original_period(pship, y, until, agreedOn);
        effect create(bba_adjustment_period_ends(pship, y, until));
    };
}
// TECH_GAP: section 6235(a)(2)-(3)'s own 270/330-day alternative "later of"
// branches (tied to a section 6225(c) modification submission date or a
// section 6231(a)(2) NOPPA date, respectively) are NOT modeled as
// SEPARATE `bba_adjustment_period_ends` tuples — the same "no max-over-
// derived" limitation `04-limitations.law`'s header already documents for
// a second `assessment_period_ends`-style tuple applies identically here;
// (c)(4)-(6) (executed-return exclusion, section 6501(c)(8)/(10) linkage)
// are not modeled either.

// ============================================================================
// §6241 — Definitions and special rules (partial)
// ============================================================================

@source(IRC_S6241, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "The term \"partnership\" means any partnership required to file a return under section 6031(a).")
pub relation bba_partnership(pship: Partnership) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "section 6241(1): scope declaration only — this package reads `Partnership` (`us.irc.core::Partnership`, the entity `us.irc.partnerships` operates on) as already meaning a section 6031(a) return-filing partnership; not independently computed";
}
rule S6241PartnershipScope strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    when us.irc.partnerships::is_partner(_, pship);
    then bba_partnership(pship);
}
@source(IRC_S6241, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "The running of any period of limitations provided in this subchapter on making a partnership adjustment (or provided by section 6501 or 6502 on the assessment or collection of any imputed underpayment determined under this subchapter) shall, in a case under title 11 of the United States Code, be suspended during the period during which the Secretary is prohibited by reason of such case from making the adjustment (or assessment or collection) and—")
pub relation bba_period_suspended_for_bankruptcy(pship: Partnership, start: Date, prohibitedThrough: Date) kind institutional {
    label en official "section 6241(6)(A): the section 6235 adjustment period (and, per its cross-reference, the section 6501/6502 assessment/collection periods for the resulting imputed underpayment) is suspended, for EVERY taxable year of the partnership then open, for the title 11 prohibition period plus 60 days (adjustment/assessment side; the +6-months collection side is `collection`'s own norm, a typed institutional dependency, mirroring `05-suspension.law`'s own §6503(h) split) — this relation is not keyed by taxable year because the bankruptcy prohibition is partnership-wide, not year-specific";
}
rule S6241SuspendedDuringBankruptcyProhibitionPlusSixtyDays strict {
    for pship: Partnership;
    for start: Date;
    for prohibitedThrough: Date;
    when bankruptcy_case_pending(pship, prohibitedThrough)
        and bankruptcy_case_started_bba(pship, start);
    then bba_period_suspended_for_bankruptcy(pship, start, add_calendar_period(prohibitedThrough, 60 calendar_day));
}
pub relation bankruptcy_case_started_bba(pship: Partnership, start: Date) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "the section 6241(6) analogue of `05-suspension.law`'s `bankruptcy_case_started`, kept separate because that relation is keyed to `Person` generally and a `Partnership` is a `Person` subtype but this package does not assume the SAME case-fact instance names both without an explicit bridge (a partnership's own title-11 case is a distinct fact from an individual partner's)";
}
// TECH_GAP/NON_NORMATIVE: §6241(2)-(5), (7)-(12) (partnership-adjustment/
// partnership-related-item scope declarations beyond (1), return due date,
// nondeductibility of payments, principal-place-of-business-abroad rule,
// (6)(B) judicial-review suspension, cessation-of-existence rule, entity-
// misclassification extension, coordination with other chapters, e-filing
// authority, special enforcement matters, CFC/PFIC partner treatment) are
// NOT modeled — definitional and administrative provisions with no
// independent computation this stage performs; each is its own coverage
// row (NON_NORMATIVE or TECH_GAP as appropriate), not silently dropped.
